  "context": "Review 2026-10-31: Cloud _execute_insert is clickhouse/client.py:271-281; clickhouse_cloud.py:379-387 falls back to super().load_data without staging, and ClickHouseNativeHandler emits server-side file() SQL (base/data_loading.py:1763-1773) that cannot read client-local files — the fix must use client-side insert_file/insert_arrow. clickhouse-connect 1.8.0 is already a dependency. Live verification of server mode needs the UAT memory-admission fix.\n\n2026-11-10 live (mocker clickhouse-server 25.8, CLICKHOUSE_MEMORY_LIMIT=4g, make heavy-run + uat-bring-up, admitted; stack torn down, mocker ps and container ls -a clean). TPC-H dbgen files, sha256 row parity vs dbgen. BEFORE (row loader, integration head e4f6854b74): SF0.01 CSV parity MISMATCH all 8 tables (loader str.strip dropped leading whitespace in comments), 8 tables load 1.14s adapter. AFTER (HTTP byte stream): SF0.01 CSV parity MATCH all 8 tables; SF0.1 CSV 866,602 rows load 10.29s -> 0.59s adapter (12.3s -> 2.6s wall incl. connect/merge settle), parity MATCH all 8 tables (lineitem 600,572). SF0.01 Parquet (customer, lineitem, nation, orders, 76,700 rows): 0.57s -> 0.10s, parity MATCH. A first AFTER run showed the server's CSV parser trimming whitespace (nation/part/... MISMATCH); fixed by input_format_csv_trim_whitespaces=0 and rerun. ClickHouse Cloud path (clickhouse_connect raw_insert) covered by unit tests only: live cloud not approved, check NOT RUN.",
